Do not define ADDRESS_SANITIZER in memory_tool.h

Chromium's ASan build already defines the ADDRESS_SANITIZER macro, so
the build fails:
  memory_tool.h:31:10: error: 'ADDRESS_SANITIZER' macro redefined
  [-Werror,-Wmacro-redefined]

Chromium commits 8740b09 (comments the line out) and 8d71305 (deletes
it) in libunwindstack.git.

diff --git a/src/libartbase/base/memory_tool.h b/src/libartbase/base/memory_tool.h
index 675ceb2..4e6cf57 100644
--- a/src/libartbase/base/memory_tool.h
+++ b/src/libartbase/base/memory_tool.h
@@ -28,7 +28,6 @@ namespace art {
 #if __has_feature(address_sanitizer)
 
 # include <sanitizer/asan_interface.h>
-# define ADDRESS_SANITIZER
 
 # ifdef ART_ENABLE_ADDRESS_SANITIZER
 #  define MEMORY_TOOL_MAKE_NOACCESS(p, s) __asan_poison_memory_region(p, s)
